            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I think this behaviour is not quite ideal: When using `gopls` (and possibly other LSPs) it has any buffer in the workspace with diagnostics open as an unlisted buffer. I can not properly open those and afaict there is no way to instruct mini.files to list them. I end up running `:e` every time.\r\n> \r\n> I'd like to request an option to list previously unlisted buffers when opening from `mini.files`. I'm also open to work on this myself if you concur about the inclusion in principle but don't want to spend the time on it :)\r\n\r\nThis definitely won't be an extra plugin option. Maybe as an extra `ensure_listed_file` for `MiniFiles.go_in()`, though.\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, this effect is possible to achieve for 99% of cases with this approach:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal go_in_with_edit = function()\r\n  local fs_entry = MiniFiles.get_fs_entry()\r\n  if fs_entry.fs_type ~= 'file' then return MiniFiles.go_in() end\r\n  vim.fn.win_execute(MiniFiles.get_target_window(), 'edit ' .. vim.fn.fnameescape(fs_entry.path))\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\r\n  callback = function(data)\r\n    vim.keymap.set('n', 'l', go_in_with_edit, { buffer = data.buf, desc = 'Go in with edit' })\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```",
